<title>EGYPT: Egyptian Gulf Bank expands new mutual fund.</title>
<headline>Egyptian Gulf Bank expands new mutual fund.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Egyptian Gulf Bank said on Thursday it was increasing the target size of its new mutual fund to 100 million pounds ($29.5 million) from 50 million because of the high demand for units.</p>
<p>It will stop taking subscriptions to the fund as soon as the 100 million pounds is covered, it added.</p>
<p>The fund is a capital growth and income mutual fund concentrating on Egyptian equities. It is the 14th launched on the Egyptian market in the past three years.</p>
<p>-- Cairo newsroom +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
</text>
